# Agent Core Principles

Fundamental software architecture and engineering principles. Stack-agnostic. Applicable to any project, language, or platform.

**Contract:** This document is the binding contract for any coding agent on this project. When existing code conflicts with these rules, **these rules prevail**. Ask before implementing when required foundations are missing — never assume.

## New Project Checklist

Before writing the first line of code, confirm:

- [ ] Layers are defined with documented responsibilities
- [ ] Core entities and aggregates are identified
- [ ] Value Objects are listed with their invariants
- [ ] Business rules are written in GIVEN/WHEN/THEN language
- [ ] State machines are documented with valid transitions
- [ ] Access roles and the permission matrix are defined
- [ ] Domain events are cataloged
- [ ] Use cases are documented with actor, flow, and preconditions
- [ ] API contract is drafted
- [ ] Domain glossary exists

If any item is blank, **ask the user before implementing**.
